---
title: DownLostFrontend · lost up
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    classDef ok stroke-width:1.6px
    classDef wait stroke-width:1.6px
    classDef fail stroke-width:1.6px

    [*] --> stop : first select saw running
    stop --> confirm : owner answers
    stop --> reselect : owner left stop unanswered
    reselect --> reselect : poll while settling
    reselect --> exiting : settling at bound
    exiting --> reselect : owner exited, rerun
    reselect --> confirm : [absent]
    reselect --> recover : [exited, ready]
    reselect --> retire : [exited, retained]
    reselect --> midstop : exited mid-stop
    recover --> confirm : death proved
    retire --> confirm : death proved
    confirm --> done : [stopped]
    confirm --> torn : [not stopped]
    done --> [*]

    note right of reselect
        HACK-2097: wait at most 15 s
        while the owner finishes its
        own stop and retires its
        publication. Never recovered
        while running or uncertain.
    end note
    note right of done
        Data retained, frontend
        shutdown recovered; hack up
        starts the run again.
    end note
    note left of midstop
        Died during its own stop:
        refusal names the explicit
        dead-owner cleanup.
    end note
    note left of torn
        INV NoDeadEnd: every refusal
        names a working step.
    end note

    class done ok
    class reselect wait
    class recover wait
    class retire wait
    class exiting wait
    class midstop fail
    class torn fail
